* sg13g2-bandgap -- sg13cmos5l-core-open-loop-bias bench body for the
* `klt sim` harness (issue #337, Part of #322). Instantiated by
* sim/sg13cmos5l-core-open-loop-bias/run_klt_sim.sh, which substitutes
* @@OSDI_DIR@@. The legacy sed-template (tb_sg13cmos5l_core_open_loop_bias
* .spice.tmpl, still the generator of every committed record) is the source
* of every device line below: same instance names, same node names, same
* W/L/a/p/m, same open-loop bias fixture -- only the harness-owned cards
* moved (see "What moved" below).
*
* DUT: design/sg13cmos5l/netlist/bandgap_core.spice, device-for-device. The
* only additions are the two fixtures the legacy template documents
* (FIXTURE 1 open-loop mirror bias, FIXTURE 2 0 V ammeters).
*
* `klt sim` netlist-body convention (klt sim --help, "Netlist convention"):
* this file is a circuit BODY. What moved out of the legacy template:
*   - the three `.lib` corner cards (cornerPNP / cornerMOShv / cornerRES):
*     the request's `models.lib` selects them per process corner, see
*     sim/harness/cmos5l_klt.py CORNER_SECTIONS;
*   - `.options temp=T tnom=27`: `klt sim` emits the corner's `.temp` card
*     and tnom defaults to 27;
*   - the `.op` analysis card and its `print`: the request's `analysis` and
*     `measurements` replace them (ngspice has no `.MEASURE OP`, so the
*     request uses a short single-step transient plus `.meas tran ... at=`,
*     the documented substitute -- sim/harness/README.md).
*
* ONE DELIBERATE DEVIATION, same as every `klt sim` body in this repo: the
* `.control` block below. SG13CMOS5L's MOS and resistor compact models are
* OSDI (PSP103 / r3_cmc, shipped prebuilt by the old pin; at the target pin
* they must be source-built -- sim/pdk-sg13cmos5l.json "osdi_toolchain") and
* must be loaded by `pre_osdi` BEFORE the netlist is parsed; `klt sim`'s
* generated `.control` block has no extension point for an engine preload
* command (filed upstream, klayout-tools#2666 -- sim/harness/README.md
* "Upstream friction").
.control
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/r3_cmc.osdi
.endc

* Supply/ground. `Vvdd`'s dc value is a placeholder: `klt sim` overrides it
* per corner with an `alter Vvdd=<v>` card from the request's
* `corners.supply_v` axis, which is why the rail has to be a named,
* alterable element.
Vvdd vdd 0 dc 3.30
Vvss vss 0 dc 0
* bandgap_core.spice wires both rppd bulk terminals to the global substrate
* net `sub!`; tied to vss through a 0 V source, as in the legacy template.
Vsub sub! vss dc 0

* FIXTURE 1 -- open-loop mirror bias: a diode-connected replica of the
* mirror device carrying 5 uA sets the shared gate net (isolates the core's
* own PTAT/CTAT generation from amplifier loop dynamics; the closed-loop
* counterpart is sg13cmos5l-closed-loop-startup).
XM0 fb fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
Ibias fb vss dc 5u

* DUT mirror legs, geometry verbatim from
* design/sg13cmos5l/netlist/bandgap_core.spice.
* FIXTURE 2 -- each leg's drain reaches its DUT node through a 0 V source,
* used purely as an ammeter (a short at DC; does not move the operating
* point).
XM1 m1d fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
Vm1 m1d sns1 dc 0
XM2 m2d fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
Vm2 m2d sns2 dc 0
XM3 m3d fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
Vm3 m3d vref dc 0

* Grounded-collector pnpMPA legs (base+collector at vss, emitter driven by
* the mirror) -- V(E)-V(B) with the base grounded, so v(sns1)/v(e2)/v(e3)
* themselves ARE VEB.
XQ1 vss vss sns1 pnpMPA a={ 1u * 2u } p={ ( 1u + 2u ) * 2 } m=1
XR2 sns2 e2 sub! rppd w=2u l=85.1u m=1 b=0
XQ2 vss vss e2 pnpMPA a={ 1u * 2u } p={ ( 1u + 2u ) * 2 } m=8
XR1 vref e3 sub! rppd w=2u l=647.0u m=1 b=0
XQ3 vss vss e3 pnpMPA a={ 1u * 2u } p={ ( 1u + 2u ) * 2 } m=1
